-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Last Stand
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Last Stand: 90 sec cooldown by default, and also reduces damage
--           taken by 30%."
--
-- Stock Last Stand grants 30% of maximum health for 20 seconds on a 3 minute
-- cooldown, and then takes the health back.  Temporary maximum health is the
-- weakest form of a defensive cooldown: it does not reduce the incoming damage,
-- so against anything that can actually kill you it buys a fixed number of
-- points once, and healing done into that window is thrown away when the buff
-- drops.  Adding flat mitigation makes the button worth pressing before the
-- spike rather than after it, and halving the cooldown puts it on the same
-- rotational footing as Shield Wall (woa_2026_08_09_03.sql).
--
-- The cooldown lives on the CATEGORY, not the spell.  12975 has
-- RecoveryTime = 0 and CategoryRecoveryTime = 180000 under category 1251, so
-- setting RecoveryTime would silently do nothing.  Category cooldowns still
-- accept SPELLMOD_COOLDOWN (Player.cpp:10986-10989) as long as the spell does
-- not carry SPELL_ATTR6_NO_CATEGORY_COOLDOWN_MODS, which 12975 does not.
--
-- The mitigation goes on the aura (12976), not the trigger (12975).  12975 is
-- SPELL_EFFECT_DUMMY, handled by core's spell_warr_last_stand
-- (src/server/scripts/Spells/spell_warrior.cpp:232), which casts 12976 with a
-- computed base point.  Effect2 on 12976 was free.
--
-- 12976's Effect1 amount is written by that script at cast time, so its base
-- points are 0 and "$s1" would render "0%".  The health half therefore stays as
-- literal prose while the new mitigation, which is a real DBC value, uses $s2.
-- (See the tooltip-variable notes in CLAUDE.md.)
--
-- Spells:
--   12975 = Last Stand (the DUMMY trigger + the cooldown)
--   12976 = Last Stand (the aura the player actually carries)
-- ============================================================

